{"base_rate":0.4926372155287818,"brier":0.1476016064257028,"bss":0.4094655213949754,"bss_hi":0.5067112643376699,"bss_lo":0.309703425753229,"chart":{"base":[487.9,132.9],"fp":[434.6,382.5],"lead":"62,191.3 272,183.4 482,176.3 692,148.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.41 — higher than 77% of cities","fp":"low end +14pp, high end -6pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.7 °C — better than 10% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 7%; promised 96% → rained 95%"},"rel":"65.4,436.3 123.3,290.7 414.2,75.4 666.8,53.5"},"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16214190093708167,"ess":208.9088905465778,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Vancouver</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Vancouver rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>95%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 747 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBURNABY 3.6 S, 11.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.41, ranked 50 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(20&ndash;96) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>163</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>113</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>97</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>95%</b></td><td class='num'>155</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Vancouver</b> <span class=\"muted\">Canada</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;49% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 49% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.41</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>20&ndash;96\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>747 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Vancouver &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Vancouver\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 62.69911504424779,369.11504424778764 73.91175257731959,351.8855670103098 117.06465753424658,287.26027397260276 205.96243243243245,190.1621621621622 307.275,88.77777777777777 397.8171612903226,22.69677419354838 397.8171612903226,43.83225806451611 307.275,164.61111111111111 205.96243243243245,268.8648648648649 117.06465753424658,352.0821917808219 73.91175257731959,378.2474226804124 62.69911504424779,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"202.6800535475234\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"202.6800535475234\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,364.13496932515335 62.69911504424779,346.56637168141594 73.91175257731959,299.44329896907215 117.06465753424658,147.64383561643834 205.96243243243245,57.351351351351354 307.275,48.33333333333337 397.8171612903226,34.438709677419354\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 163 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"364.13496932515335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 113 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"62.69911504424779\" cy=\"346.56637168141594\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 97 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"73.91175257731959\" cy=\"299.44329896907215\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 17%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"117.06465753424658\" cy=\"147.64383561643834\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 42%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"205.96243243243245\" cy=\"57.351351351351354\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 92% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"307.275\" cy=\"48.33333333333337\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 95% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 155 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"397.8171612903226\" cy=\"34.438709677419354\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(49%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Vancouver the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.53) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.24).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>210</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.242</td><td class='num'>20.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>0.279</td><td class='num'>20.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>0.442</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.532</td><td class='num'>7.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":49.24966,"lon":-123.11934,"n":747,"n_cities":216,"name":"Vancouver","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":163,"obs":0.049079754601226995,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.01327433628318584,"n":113,"obs":0.09734513274336283,"sig":true},{"hi":0.09,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.044948453608247424,"n":97,"obs":0.2268041237113402,"sig":true},{"hi":0.28,"lo":0.09,"mean":0.16684931506849318,"n":73,"obs":0.6438356164383562,"sig":true},{"hi":0.59,"lo":0.28,"mean":0.41797297297297303,"n":74,"obs":0.8918918918918919,"sig":true},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.59,"mean":0.7041666666666666,"n":72,"obs":0.9166666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9599354838709678,"n":155,"obs":0.9548387096774194,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":11.4,"provisional":false,"rank":50,"rank_hi":96.02499999999998,"rank_lo":19.975,"reliability":0.05473028189504427,"resolution":0.15542690465029485,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"vancouver","station":"BURNABY 3.6 S","timezone":"America/Vancouver"}